      "message": "High-Level Review \u0026 Target Structure for coordinate_descent_minimizer_test.cc\n\nThe split between ordering tests (CoordinateDescentMinimizerOrdering) and solve tests (CoordinateDescentMinimizerTest), as well as the RestoresBlockMetadata matcher, is heading in the right direction, but the fixture design and two of the test cases still have structural and correctness issues:\n\n1. Consolidate setup ceremony inside CoordinateDescentMinimizerTest:\n- Currently, every TEST_F repeats the same 8 lines of setup (IsOrderingValid, CreateMinimizer, RecordMetadata, NumParameters() \u003d\u003d state_.size()), calls CreateMinimizer() before RecordMetadata() (which has the hidden side effect of calling SetParameterOffsetsAndIndex()), and manually duplicates initial parameter values into state_ (e.g., setting both z_ \u003d 1.0 and state_ \u003d {0.0, 1.0}).\n- Fix the fixture so that a single bool InitMinimizer(const ParameterBlockOrdering\u0026 ordering) method performs the full initialization in the right order:\n  1. Calls problem_.mutable_program()-\u003eSetParameterOffsetsAndIndex().\n  2. Resizes state_ to problem_.program().NumParameters(), populates it via problem_.program().ParameterBlocksToStateVector(state_.data()), and saves initial_state_ \u003d state_.\n  3. Records metadata_ into a fixture member std::vector\u003cBlockMetadata\u003e metadata_.\n  4. Initializes a fixture member CoordinateDescentMinimizer minimizer_{problem_.context()} via minimizer_.Init(problem_.program(), problem_.parameter_map(), ordering, \u0026error_).\n- Provide void ResetState() { state_ \u003d initial_state_; } and void Minimize(int num_threads \u003d 1) on the fixture.\n- Do not call IsOrderingValid in the TEST_F solve tests; it is already tested in CoordinateDescentMinimizerOrdering.\n- Keep all ASSERT_TRUE(InitMinimizer(ordering)) \u003c\u003c error_;, EXPECT_THAT(...), and EXPECT_NEAR(...) assertions directly in the test bodies.\n\n2. Ensure metadata-restoration tests exercise non-zero block offsets:\n- During CoordinateDescentMinimizer::Minimize, the inner solve temporarily sets index \u003d 0, delta_offset \u003d 0, and state_offset \u003d 0 on the active ParameterBlock.\n- For the first parameter block in a program (parameter_blocks()[0]), index, delta_offset, and state_offset are already 0. Testing metadata restoration when only block 0 is optimized is therefore vacuous (it passes even if Minimize never restores the metadata).\n- Both RepeatedMinimizationRestoresMetadataAfterStateReset and KeepsExcludedParameterBlockFixed currently only optimize block 0. Update both so that a parameter block at a non-zero offset (index 1, offset 1) is optimized.\n\n3. Use ParameterBlockOrdering APIs directly in ordering tests:\n- Use ordering-\u003eNumElements(), ordering-\u003eNumGroups(), and ordering-\u003eGroupSize(...) instead of manually iterating over group_to_elements().",
